{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And it shall become dust upon all the land of Egypt</b> — According to the opinion of our Sages (Exodus Rabbah 10:6), from that soot there descended dust upon all the land of Egypt, and when that dust descended upon man and beast throughout all the land of Egypt it raised boils and blisters on them, for it was a burning heat, and perhaps the wind would also carry dust into the houses so that no one could escape it. This is correct. Similarly, it descends many times during years of drought in the form of dust when the dew falls, as it is written (Deuteronomy 28:24), 'HaShem will make the rain of your land dust and earth.' And likewise it is possible to say, according to the plain sense, that the meaning of <b>and it shall become dust</b> is that the dust produced from the soot in its place would inflict boils upon all the land of Egypt, for it smote the air to do thus, and it is a decree from on High:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:04:53.805138562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}